{"id":"googie-kitsch","title":"Googie Kitsch","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Googie_Kitsch","rev":239866,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Googie Kitsch"]}," is the revival of the playful side of ",{"t":"a","c":["mid-century modern"],"id":"mid-century-modern"}," design (eg. colorful George Nelson clocks, boomerang tables), Googie motifs, general 1950s-60s advertising vernacular & pop culture kitsch. It emerged in hip ",{"t":"a","c":["Pacific Punk Wave"],"id":"pacific-punk-wave"}," design circles mainly in the late 1970s, spreading in various forms & fields throughout the late 20th century, before peaking in the ",{"t":"a","c":["Y2K Futurism"],"id":"y2k-futurism"}," era of the late 1990s and early 2000s."]},{"t":"p","c":["This style overlaps with ",{"t":"a","c":["Diner Kitsch"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Diner_Kitsch"},", though that aesthetic mainly pulls from older American diners from the 1930s-50s built in the ",{"t":"a","c":["Streamline Moderne"],"id":"streamline-moderne"}," style. The 1990s 'lounge' revival also overlapped with Googie Kitsch, pulling from sources such as 1960s bachelor pad style, exotica & tiki culture, Space Age pop music, etc."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The aesthetic draws inspiration from the \"Jetsons\" cartoon where it presents the future as an automated, fun utopia of flying cars and plastic modular spaces along with its hyper-commercial neon motifs focusing on flashy, animated neon, bold signage, and massive pylons, designed with a space age and an atomic twist where complete physics breakthroughs and saturation of space icons, such as shooting stars, abstract diagrams of atoms, parabolas and starbursts."]},{"t":"p","c":["Gravity-defying, asymmetrical geometry incorporates heavy use of cantilevered steel, upswept roofs, iconic \"boomerang\" pillars, sharp structural angles, or tables with a unabashed, vibrant palettes that focus on bold primary colors, classic era shades such as flamingo pink, turquoise, and mint green."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Brands"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Sonic"]},{"c":["Jack In The Box"]},{"c":["Johnny Rockets"]},{"c":["Fabulous Fifties Cafe"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Music"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Lit"]},{"c":["Smash Mouth"]},{"c":["The Pussycat Dolls"]},{"c":["Perrey and Kingsley"]},{"c":["Les Baxter and Martin Denny"]},{"c":["The Pizzicato Five"]},{"c":["Stereolab"]},{"c":["Esquivel!"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Literature"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Archie"]},{"c":["Snoopy"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/fc/Original_28fdf60bb2386f25e8e7a0b05e8dcb46.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321041244","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/9a/Original_0d658df61a969042e69be30b4280ad70.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321041219","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a7/Original_1eba554d6849a04b6e98e0f5f5c83027.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321041152","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/6f/Sno-drift.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321041116","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/0f/Original_1db2d2d178c1a58963535d31b742d900.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321041055","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/09/Girls_room.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321040950","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/79/Dreamcast.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321040852","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/f7/Cocktail_mix.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321040828","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/0e/Esquivel.png/revision/latest?cb=20260321040806","w":185,"h":18